#: src/3641-export-function-ordinals.md:1
msgid "Feature Name: `export_function_ordinals`"
msgstr ""

#: src/3641-export-function-ordinals.md:2
msgid "Start Date: 2024-05-19"
msgstr ""

#: src/3641-export-function-ordinals.md:3
msgid ""
"RFC PR: [rust-lang/rfcs#3641](https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3641)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3641-export-function-ordinals.md:4
msgid ""
"Rust Issue: [rust-lang/rust#154022](https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/"
"issues/154022)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3641-export-function-ordinals.md:6
msgid "Summary"
msgstr ""

#: src/3641-export-function-ordinals.md:9
msgid ""
"Adding an unsafe attribute, `#[unsafe(export_ordinal(n))]`, that marks the "
"ordinal position of an exported function in a cdylib on windows targets "
"without creating a `lib.def` file."
msgstr ""

#: src/3641-export-function-ordinals.md:11
msgid "Motivation"
msgstr ""

#: src/3641-export-function-ordinals.md:14
msgid ""
"Sometimes when creating DLLs, the ordinal position of an exported function "
"is very important. For example, when creating a DLL for use in [Microsoft "
"Detours](https://github.com/microsoft/Detours/), the "
"[`DetourFinishHelperProcess`](https://github.com/microsoft/Detours/wiki/"
"DetourFinishHelperProcess) function must be Ordinal 1."
msgstr ""

#: src/3641-export-function-ordinals.md:16
msgid ""
"Rust currently has a [`link_ordinal`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/reference/"
"items/external-blocks.html#the-link_ordinal-attribute) attribute which "
"allows importing a function by its ordinal, however there is currently no "
"option to do the opposite."
msgstr ""

#: src/3641-export-function-ordinals.md:18
msgid ""
"Currently, this would be done by creating a `lib.def` file and linking it in "
"`build.rs`."
msgstr ""

#: src/3641-export-function-ordinals.md:28
msgid "// build.rs\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/3641-export-function-ordinals.md:30
msgid "\"path/to/lib.def\""
msgstr ""

#: src/3641-export-function-ordinals.md:31
msgid "\"cargo:rustc-cdylib-link-arg=/DEF:{}\""
msgstr ""

#: src/3641-export-function-ordinals.md:35
msgid ""
"The biggest downside of the current method is that once you specify a `.def` "
"file, you will have to specify an ordinal for every function that you want "
"to export from the DLL, or else it won't be present in the generated `.lib` "
"file. This can become very overwhelming if you have a lot of exported "
"functions."
msgstr ""

#: src/3641-export-function-ordinals.md:37
msgid ""
"By creating an attribute for specifying function ordinals, we can choose the "
"ordinal position for the functions where it matters, and let Rust choose the "
"ordinal for any other functions where ordinal position is not important."
msgstr ""

#: src/3641-export-function-ordinals.md:39
msgid "Guide-level explanation"
msgstr ""

#: src/3641-export-function-ordinals.md:42
msgid "Ordinals"
msgstr ""

#: src/3641-export-function-ordinals.md:44
msgid ""
"Function Ordinals refer to the position of an exported function in a "
"Dynamically Linked Library (DLL). When accessing functions by name, this is "
"not important. However some applications access functions based on their "
"position (ordinal), rather than their name. The Microsoft documentation for "
"this concept is available [here.](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/cpp/"
"build/exporting-functions-from-a-dll-by-ordinal-rather-than-by-name)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3641-export-function-ordinals.md:46
msgid "Usage"
msgstr ""

#: src/3641-export-function-ordinals.md:48
msgid ""
"You can specify the ordinality of an exported function using the "
"`export_ordinal` attribute on it. The attribute must be marked as unsafe."
msgstr ""

#: src/3641-export-function-ordinals.md:52
#: src/3641-export-function-ordinals.md:95
msgid "\"C\""
msgstr ""

#: src/3641-export-function-ordinals.md:53
msgid "\"Hello, World!\""
msgstr ""

#: src/3641-export-function-ordinals.md:57
msgid ""
"This example will export `hello` as ordinal 1, and when a program tries to "
"call ordinal 1 in your DLL, it will be executed."
msgstr ""

#: src/3641-export-function-ordinals.md:59
msgid "Behaviour"
msgstr ""

#: src/3641-export-function-ordinals.md:61
msgid ""
"If other software expects your function to be a specific ordinal, you should "
"be very careful when changing the ordinal or removing the `export_ordinal` "
"attribute, as it could lead to the wrong function being called (or not found "
"at all)."
msgstr ""

#: src/3641-export-function-ordinals.md:63
msgid ""
"If `export_ordinal` isn't provided, an unused ordinal will be assigned "
"during compilation."
msgstr ""

#: src/3641-export-function-ordinals.md:65
msgid "Reference-level explanation"
msgstr ""

#: src/3641-export-function-ordinals.md:68
msgid ""
"`export_ordinal` is a new attribute for functions which has a signature "
"similar to the following:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3641-export-function-ordinals.md:74
msgid "`n` must be:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3641-export-function-ordinals.md:76
msgid "A positive integer >= 1"
msgstr ""

#: src/3641-export-function-ordinals.md:77
msgid "Unique across the entire program."
msgstr ""

#: src/3641-export-function-ordinals.md:78
msgid ""
"An error should be thrown if the same ordinal is provided in multiple places."
msgstr ""

#: src/3641-export-function-ordinals.md:80
msgid ""
"The attribute should only affect windows targets, as ordinals are not a "
"feature of shared libraries on other targets."
msgstr ""

#: src/3641-export-function-ordinals.md:82
msgid "The attribute must be marked as unsafe."
msgstr ""

#: src/3641-export-function-ordinals.md:84
msgid "The attribute must be placed above an exported function like so:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3641-export-function-ordinals.md:90
msgid "// Also works with extern and unsafe functions\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/3641-export-function-ordinals.md:98
msgid "Drawbacks"
msgstr ""

#: src/3641-export-function-ordinals.md:101
msgid ""
"Specifying ordinals in code could add a lot of additional complexity with "
"linking."
msgstr ""

#: src/3641-export-function-ordinals.md:103
msgid "Rationale and alternatives"
msgstr ""

#: src/3641-export-function-ordinals.md:106
msgid ""
"This design is consistent with the [`link_ordinal`](https://doc.rust-lang."
"org/reference/items/external-blocks.html#the-link_ordinal-attribute) "
"attribute already in use."
msgstr ""

#: src/3641-export-function-ordinals.md:108
msgid ""
"The attribute is marked as unsafe as it shares the same concerns as "
"`export_name`, which is [unsafe as of Rust 2024 Edition](https://github.com/"
"ehuss/edition-guide/blob/b80cba8af64a9c52d56f7081c764e5396e406f6c/src/"
"rust-2024/unsafe-attributes.md)."
msgstr ""

#: src/3641-export-function-ordinals.md:110
msgid "Some considered alternatives are:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3641-export-function-ordinals.md:112
msgid ""
"Do nothing; keep using the `.def` files with `cargo:rustc-cdylib-link-arg=/"
"DEF`"
msgstr ""

#: src/3641-export-function-ordinals.md:113
msgid ""
"The main downside of doing nothing and using the `.def` file, is that if you "
"only need one function with a specific ordinal, you have to add every "
"exported function to the `.def` file or they won't be linkable."
msgstr ""

#: src/3641-export-function-ordinals.md:114
msgid "Use macros to generate a `.def` file"
msgstr ""

#: src/3641-export-function-ordinals.md:115
msgid "A good implementation of this would likely require stateful macros."
msgstr ""

#: src/3641-export-function-ordinals.md:116
msgid ""
"Implement a way to provide a `.def` file without also having to specify "
"every other exported function inside it."
msgstr ""

#: src/3641-export-function-ordinals.md:117
msgid ""
"This would be a good alternative, although the implementation could be more "
"complicated."
msgstr ""

#: src/3641-export-function-ordinals.md:119
msgid ""
"This proposal should make the workflow of specifying ordinals much easier, "
"while staying consistent with the syntax of the existing `link_ordinal`."
msgstr ""

#: src/3641-export-function-ordinals.md:121
msgid "Prior art"
msgstr ""

#: src/3641-export-function-ordinals.md:124
msgid ""
"I am not currently aware of any programming languages that currently "
"implement an equivalent feature."
msgstr ""

#: src/3641-export-function-ordinals.md:126
msgid "Unresolved questions"
msgstr ""

#: src/3641-export-function-ordinals.md:129
msgid "Some unresolved questions are:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3641-export-function-ordinals.md:130
msgid ""
"Can ordinals be skipped? If you specify ordinals `1, 3, 4`, should this "
"throw an error as `2` is skipped?"
msgstr ""

#: src/3641-export-function-ordinals.md:131
msgid ""
"If ordinals `1, 3` are specified, and you have another exported function, "
"should it use `2` (the next unused ordinal) or `4` (the next in the "
"sequence)?"
msgstr ""

#: src/3641-export-function-ordinals.md:132
msgid ""
"Instead of implementing this proposal, Could the usage of the `.def` file be "
"changed to allow other functions to stay exported, even if they aren't "
"included in the `.def` file?"
msgstr ""

#: src/3641-export-function-ordinals.md:134
msgid "Future possibilities"
msgstr ""

#: src/3641-export-function-ordinals.md:137
msgid "I cannot currently think of any future possibilities."
msgstr ""
